      "research_question": "Does block-trade activity (amount share over 5 days, count intensity over 20 days) predict negative 5-day returns because block trades clear at discounts and signal large-holder supply?",
      "mechanism": "Block trades are negotiated at discounts and mostly reflect large-holder distribution; the event table is announcement-dated and p1_events lags it one trading day, so the features are PIT-safe. High block-trade intensity should predict underperformance; candidates are oriented high = low block intensity. Event flow is zero-filled (true zero) upstream.",
